From 8e0c9b38827a505163792f0307e5711a64e31019 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 03:41:22 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] test(post): derive the per-post conformance rows from the
 registry

A new post added rows to shared tables in two test files. Two new-post
branches conflicted in crates/app/tests/conformance.rs. In
crates/post/tests/comment_escape.rs they each raised the fixed count of
text posts by one; that merged with no conflict to a count one too low,
and main went red.

conformance.rs now takes its rows from the app registry
(posting::BUILTINS and its LATHE / PLASMA / WIRE / SINKER lists). A
milling dialect is each entry that no other family lists, except
Klartext. The extension check reads each post's own manifest line and
expects nc. A short sorted table names only the posts whose control
reads another file type. The registry check now asserts a partition:
unique names, a shipped file for each, each entry in one family, and
Fanuc as entry 0.

comment_escape.rs counts the .cps files that it finds, not a number.

The same posts, goldens and streams are checked as before.

Refs #3461

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
